os","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-13T17:22:12Z","updated_at":"2026-10-13T17:22:12Z","body":"The AudioServer syncs objects on the process but the threaded AudioDriver requests buffer updates at random and that buffer content is what you are actually hearing as audio on your hardware. So if the server already send playback data that the driver picked up it will be played, no way to stop, and a playback that has started runs for at least 1 frame with a fadeout before it actually stops and gets deleted.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6151203494/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]